@cobasuyi , one thing worth checking in your n8n tools before the client demo: if a Webhook node that Vapi calls is set to Respond: Immediately, n8n answers “Workflow was started” before the lookup runs. The agent gets no data back and makes up an answer. It’s a one-setting fix, and it’s the first case I’d replay, the same way I replayed 120 orders in the n8n demo above. 
 I can start on your trial agent today, on the terms from my post above, and I test on a copy so your live agents stay untouched. 
 Which agent should go first?

Hi  @cobasuyi  — I’m interested in the paid one-agent QA trial. 
 My strongest fit is workflow reliability, edge-case testing and failure analysis rather than presenting myself as a Vapi/ElevenLabs voice specialist. 
 I recently completed a local n8n 2.42.5 QA project where I imported and executed multiple AI workflows and built a reproducible test harness around them. 
 A few examples of issues I found and fixed: 
 - a workflow that could not import because the top-level workflow ID was missing; 
 - an HTTP/OpenAI request expression that was silently truncated by the n8n expression parser, so the intended live node had never actually sent a request; 
 - retry behaviour that did not match the original documentation, verified with mixed-failure and all-failure tests; 
 - item-linking and multi-branch checks to make sure records were neither lost nor duplicated. 
 Validation result: 5 complete executions, 54 assertions, 0 failures, with screenshots and reproducible evidence files. 
 For your agent I’d deliver: 
 - normal + edge-case test matrix; 
 - API/webhook and malformed-input tests; 
 - timeout/retry/fallback checks; 
 - AI output / JSON validation checks; 
 - severity-ranked findings; 
 - reproducible failure cases; 
 - Demo Ready / Not Demo Ready verdict. 
 To be transparent, I don’t claim production Vapi/Twilio/ElevenLabs experience, so I’d keep voice-specific tuning outside scope unless you want interface-behaviour testing only. 
 Timezone: UTC+8. 
 For a bounded first pilot, I can start at USD 75 fixed, or USD 18/hour if the scope is not defined yet.

