Hi  @cobasuyi , 
 I’m Isaac Palomino Álvarez, a Solutions Architect based in Madrid (CEST / UTC+2). I can take one existing agent through a bounded pre-demo QA trial without redesigning it. 
  Rate and trial:  EUR 240 fixed for one agreed agent path, or EUR 40/hour. Delivery within three business days after scope, a credential-free workflow export, representative payloads and test access are available. 
  What I would test:  

 malformed, missing and conflicting inputs; 
 duplicate or out-of-order webhook delivery; 
 provider 4xx/5xx, 429, timeout and partial-success cases; 
 retries after an external side effect may already have happened; 
 malformed LLM/tool output, unsupported claims and unsafe actions; 
 call interruption, silence and human-handoff paths where applicable; 
 whether every failure is observable, recoverable and safe to replay. 

 The important distinction is between  rejected before acceptance  (safe to retry),  accepted but response lost  (ambiguous; route to review), and  duplicate delivery  (must produce one external effect). I verify effects at the provider/target system, not from a green n8n execution alone. 
  Deliverables:  an agreed test matrix of up to 15 scenarios, expected-versus-actual evidence, severity-ranked findings, reproduction steps, a prioritized fix plan, one contained fix where feasible, and a retest. You keep the original workflow untouched until a change is approved. 
  Relevant experience:  five years with n8n, API/webhook integrations and AI automation, plus more than five AI/LLM projects delivered in a prior company setting. My strongest depth is n8n, OpenAI/Claude, structured outputs, workflow reliability, auditability and human review. I won’t overstate provider-specific experience: I do not have a published production case specifically for Vapi/Twilio/ElevenLabs, so I would validate their contracts, logs, latency, retries and failure behaviour from real payloads rather than claim voice-stack specialization. 
  Technical portfolio:   Production n8n Workflow Systems — Ascendia Intelligence  
